@doc <PREFIX>-ARCH [std, active, agents+employees, machine-drafted] v1
## <Structure in one line: module count and names, the governing pattern, and the dependency direction.>
@links <PREFIX>-OVERVIEW,<PREFIX>-DEPS,<PREFIX>-STANDARDS
@anchor [repo:<repo-name>, vcs:git]
  + <source glob, e.g. src/<Project>.*/**>
  ! **/*.Tests/**
  ! **/bin/**
  ! **/obj/**
@cycle 90d
@reviewed <YYYY-MM-DD from git log for the anchored paths>

@def architecture
  Continuous prose. How the modules divide responsibility, which way dependencies point, where the
  composition root is, and which abstractions are ports versus adapters. State the dependency
  direction explicitly — it is the claim the contradiction check validates.

@props <group-name>
  + <ServiceOrType>  | <its job in one line>
  + <ServiceOrType>  | <its job in one line>

@props <public-surface>
  + <Controller / route / export>  | <what it exposes>

@rules
  1. <Imperative, independently actionable. "Controllers are dispatch-only; orchestration lives in X.">
  2. <Something an agent could otherwise get wrong.>
  3. <A fail-safe behavior worth stating: what happens below a threshold, on timeout, on conflict.>

@constraints
  <slug>
  requires: <the dependency-direction invariant — this is checked mechanically against the manifests>
  forbids:  <a state or action that is unconditionally prohibited>
  enforced-by: <code-review | analyzer | CI gate | named standard>

@status
  known-gap: <architectural debt an agent should not mistake for intent>
